      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOPP: Thank you, and Mr. Chief Justice,\nand may it please the Court:\nThis case involves the fundamental First\nAmendment question of whether the Government can shield\nlawmakers from grassroots lobbying about upcoming votes\nin Congress through campaign finance laws.\nThis Court has distinguished the regulation\nof corporate electioneering from efforts to influence\nlawmaking, finding sufficiently compelling\ngovernmental interests in regulating electioneering,\nbut not grassroots lobbying."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f4f3ef01bb595392a58ff27afef859122337f9db341c9ae515ed6bab630072dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f4f3ef01bb59-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. So what is the test? Because I -- my vague recollection from a year and a half ago is that there was in that testimony political consultants who said if you really want to defeat a Senator, here's how you do it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. BOPP",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f4f3ef01bb595392a58ff27afef859122337f9db341c9ae515ed6bab630072dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f4f3ef01bb59-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that you would look at, one, whether the -- the ad discusses a current legislative issue; two, whether or not it made any reference to the legislator beyond lobbying him or her about that specific issue. So there should not be any references to the election or the candidacy of the incumbent or any of those type references."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'CONNOR",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f4f3ef01bb595392a58ff27afef859122337f9db341c9ae515ed6bab630072dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f4f3ef01bb59-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, this ad could have been run by your clients by a segregated fund."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f4f3ef01bb595392a58ff27afef859122337f9db341c9ae515ed6bab630072dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f4f3ef01bb59-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In McConnell against FEC, this Court upheld title II's definition and regulation of electioneering communications by corporations and unions as defined in the act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f4f3ef01bb595392a58ff27afef859122337f9db341c9ae515ed6bab630072dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f4f3ef01bb59-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there any other case that you can cite where we've upheld a facial challenge and then later said that an as-applied challenge was barred by our ruling on the facial challenge?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Wisconsin Republican Party",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f4f3ef01bb595392a58ff27afef859122337f9db341c9ae515ed6bab630072dd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f4f3ef01bb59-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "by the candidates opposing Senator Feingold, by the Wisconsin Republican Party, and by appellant's own PAC."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Appellant's PAC",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1581",
      "confidence": 1.0,
